<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="EL 4.0">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 is an Enapter AEM electrolyser described as the equipment in the source document. The following table contains technical specifications for the EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;The EL 4.0, also referred to as EL40, AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0, or AEM Electrolyser EL40, is an Enapter AEM electrolyser that generates hydrogen by water electrolysis and is specified by production rate, purity, output pressure, power consumption, heat dissipation, utilities, environmental limits, dimensions, weight, control interfaces, and conformity marks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5c89217037bf7757266979c0a494a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter">
  <data key="d0">Enapter</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enapter is the organization or brand named in the product designation Enapter EL 4.0 AEM electrolyser.&lt;SEP&gt;Enapter is the manufacturer of the EL 4.0 electrolyser and the provider of the EMS used for its control and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5c89217037bf7757266979c0a494a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
