  <data key="d5">1790710726</data>
</node>
<node id="Production Rate">
  <data key="d0">Production Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 production rate is up to 500 NL/h, up to 1.0785 kg/24 h.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<edge source="Hydrogen Output Purity" target="Hydrogen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The hydrogen output of the EL 4.0 has a purity of 99.9% (&lt; 1,000 ppm H₂O and &lt; 5 ppm O₂) at 25 °C at 35 barg and 98.8% (&lt; 12,000 ppm H₂O and &lt; 5 ppm O₂) at 25 °C at 8 barg.</data>
  <data key="d9">gas quality,has_parameter</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1790710787</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<node id="Output Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Output Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 output pressure is up to 35 barg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nominal Power Consumption Per Nm³ of H₂ Produced">
  <data key="d0">Nominal Power Consumption Per Nm³ of H₂ Produced</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 nominal power consumption per Nm³ of H₂ produced is 4.8 kWh/Nm³, beginning of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operative Power Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Operative Power Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 operative power consumption is 2.4 kW, beginning of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peak Power Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Peak Power Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 peak power consumption is 3 kW.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heat Dissipation">
  <data key="d0">Heat Dissipation</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 heat dissipation is 0.6 kW, beginning of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Heat Dissipation">
  <data key="d0">Max Heat Dissipation</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 max heat dissipation is 0.9 kW, end of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standby Power Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Standby Power Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 standby power consumption is 0.3 kW.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Supply">
  <data key="d0">Power Supply</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 power supply is 220 – 240 V (AC), 50/60 Hz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Water Input Conductivity">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Water Input Conductivity</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 maximum water input conductivity requirement is a minimum of ASTM D1193-06 Type IV, or recommended Type II or Type III.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Water Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 water consumption is ~ 420 mL/h at 25 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Input Pressure Range">
  <data key="d0">Water Input Pressure Range</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 water input pressure range is 1 – 4 barg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Operative Temperature Range">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Operative Temperature Range</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 ambient operative temperature range is 5 °C – 45 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Operative Humidity Range">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Operative Humidity Range</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 ambient operative humidity range is up to 90% humidity, non-condensing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IP Rating">
  <data key="d0">IP Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 IP rating is IP 20.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dimensions">
  <data key="d0">Dimensions</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 dimensions are W: 482 mm × D: 635 mm × H: 266 mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight">
  <data key="d0">Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 weight is 42 kg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Space Inside Cabinet">
  <data key="d0">Space Inside Cabinet</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 requires 6 U of space inside the cabinet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control and Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Control and Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">controlsystem</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 control and monitoring is fully automatic with Enapter's EMS via 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth and Modbus TCP over Ethernet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter's EMS">
  <data key="d0">Enapter's EMS</data>
  <data key="d1">controlsystem</data>
  <data key="d2">Enapter's EMS provides fully automatic control and monitoring of the EL 4.0 through 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth and Modbus TCP over Ethernet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conformity">
  <data key="d0">Conformity</data>
  <data key="d1">safetyrequirement</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 conformity comprises the CE mark according to the machine directive 2006/42/CE, the UKCA mark according to Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008, and CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 for hydrogen generators using water electrolysis in industrial, commercial, and residential applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CE Mark">
  <data key="d0">CE Mark</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">The CE mark is applied to the EL 4.0 according to the machine directive 2006/42/CE.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UKCA Mark">
  <data key="d0">UKCA Mark</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">The UKCA mark is applied to the EL 4.0 according to the Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1">
  <data key="d0">CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 covers hydrogen generators using water electrolysis for industrial, commercial, and residential applications and applies to the EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASTM D1193-06">
  <data key="d0">ASTM D1193-06</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">ASTM D1193-06 specifies reagent water types; Type IV is the minimum acceptable water input quality for the EL 4.0, with Type II or Type III recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen (H₂) is the product of the EL 4.0, generated at up to 500 NL/h or up to 1.0785 kg/24 h.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">utility</data>
  <data key="d2">Water is an input utility for the EL 4.0, consumed at approximately 420 mL/h at 25 °C, supplied at 1 – 4 barg and meeting a maximum conductivity requirement of minimum ASTM D1193-06 Type IV or recommended Type II or Type III.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electricity">
  <data key="d0">Electricity</data>
  <data key="d1">utility</data>
  <data key="d2">Electricity is the power input for the EL 4.0, supplied at 220 – 240 V (AC), 50/60 Hz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen (O₂) appears as an impurity in the EL 4.0 hydrogen output at less than 5 ppm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Electrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Water Electrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Water electrolysis is the process by which the EL 4.0 generates hydrogen from water.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790710769</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
